Third-party sources
-------------------

The guidance in `referencias/` adapts ideas from these sources in our own
words; no file or passage was copied. Both repositories are MIT-licensed; the
video-prompt collection gathers prompts written by many authors, who keep
their own rights, and only general techniques were taken from it. The
repositories' copyright and permission notices are reproduced here as a
courtesy.

1. marketingskills
   https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills
   Copyright (c) 2025 Corey Haines
   License: MIT
   Read at commit 1f837447b20bb6f0e72d87b80ece1c221c362c7d
   Ideas taken: hooks and opening families, ad angles, caption structure,
   calls to action by awareness stage, post archetypes.

2. awesome-opus5-5-videos
   https://github.com/yihui-dev/awesome-opus5-5-videos
   Copyright (c) 2026 yihui-dev (the collection; each prompt belongs to its author)
   License: MIT (the collection)
   Read at commit 92aee2f586ac0715cb3cbcb6384834f98a33383d
   Ideas taken: scene pacing, the cover frame, accent words, persistent shapes
   across cuts, transitions centred on the cut, end cards.
   Video styles (referencias/estilos-video/, round 7): each style file distils,
   in our own words and rebuilt for the studio's engine, techniques described
   in prompts of the collection. No prompt text was copied. Prompts read for
   them, by the author names their files carry in the collection: 0xnicc0,
   flxrnc, annacher, demonugc, dzhohola, diamai (one shape, a cursor that
   clicks, a counter); jake11moran (a list that lands, checklist ticks, an
   oversized cursor); notdwd (a typed request, nothing ever freezes);
   techhalla and twoclipping (kinetic type, the loud poster, a counter with a
   line); thegrootdev, okapi-fukugyo (a cursor operating an interface);
   brainextends, daniel-haida (the product film, one idea per shot);
   aschapmann, alex-prompter, archiveexplorer (how-it-works and objection
   beats); gdgtify (locked on-screen copy). Each prompt belongs to its author.

